chnical specifications\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026.\u2026\u20264 Table 11.1-.","platform":"airborne"},{"method":"radiometrics","page":10,"text":"The survey helped accurately map the property geology and generate exploration targets."},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":11,"text":"IP, MAG, VLF surveys) to find base metal and gold targets. Notwithstanding this problem, the report author encourages pursuing the exploration of the property aimi"},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":23,"text":"600 soil samples (B horizon) and rock samples were analyzed for Cu, Pb, Zn, and Ag.","year":1993},{"method":"magnetics","page":23,"text":"No Au and Ag values associated with altered rocks. VLF-EM and Total Field Magnetometer geophysical surveys. Report 473770. 1989 - Rio Algom Exploration Inc.","year":1989},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":23,"text":"Ltd.- Soil samples collected in an area characterized by an electromagnetic anomalous zone. Report 470823. 1989 - Novagold Resources Inc. 122 stream sediment samples and 48 rock samples collected near streams.","year":1957},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":25,"text":"Report 470819. 1979 - Mattagami Lake Mines Ltd. IP and resistivity geophysical survey over the Mable Brook area. No chargeability anomalies were detected. Report 472430. 1980 - Mattagami Lake Mines Ltd.","year":1979},{"method":"magnetics","page":25,"text":"Magnetometer and VLF surveys. EM-16 and Fraser Filter survey on a 200 x 25m grid. Prospecting, grab rock sampling."},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":25,"text":"Magnetometer and VLF surveys. EM-16 and Fraser Filter survey on a 200 x 25m grid. Prospecting, grab rock sampling.","year":1990},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":26,"text":"Soil anomalies found near zones B and C. An IP survey indicated chargeability anomalies corresponding to zones A and C mineralization."},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":26,"text":"Ltd. High-resolution airborne geophysical surveys (EM, VLF, MAG) flown over the Riley Brook 3-5-6 and Blue Mountain Lake properties.","platform":"airborne","year":1991},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":27,"text":"Report 475958. 1994 - Noranda Exploration Co. Ltd. IP survey and trenching. No significant results were reported. Report 474251.","year":1994},{"method":"magnetics","page":27,"text":"Report 475050. 2001 - Scott Mitchell. Magnetometer survey and prospecting around a historical trench. Report 475194. 6.4. Blue Mountain River 1956 - Conwest Exploration Co. Ltd.","year":2001,"platform":"airborne"},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":27,"text":"Report 475958. 1993- Noranda Exploration. Airborne and magnetic HEM, VLF-EM survey showing three favorable zones where VLF-EM conductors are crossed by east-west trending faults or magnetic trends.","platform":"airborne","year":1993},{"method":"magnetics","page":28,"text":"Geochemical survey and airborne magnetic and electromagnetic surveys. No targets were detected. Report 470820. 1976 - Amoco Canada Petroleum Co Ltd. Geochemical soil survey. No significant results.","platform":"airborne","year":1957},{"method":"magnetics","page":29,"text":"Report 474251. 1997 - Novagold Resource Inc. VLF-EM and magnetometer survey. Two anomalous zones were detected. Report 474824. 1997 - Connecticut Development Corp.","year":1997,"platform":"airborne"},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":29,"text":"Report 474251. 1997 - Novagold Resource Inc. VLF-EM and magnetometer survey. Two anomalous zones were detected. Report 474824. 1997 - Connecticut Development Corp.","year":1997,"platform":"airborne"},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":30,"text":"1992 - Novagold Resources Inc. Geophysical surveys including IP, VLF-EM, Total Field Magnetic and Gradient Magnetic. Soil sampling, prospecting.","year":1992},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":55,"text":"9.3. HeliTEM\u00b2 Electromagnetic, Magnetic and Radiometric Survey Fancamp Exploration and Lode Gold Resources under the Acadian Gold Corp.","platform":"airborne","line_km":322.2},{"method":"magnetics","page":59,"text":"This method enhances regions of discontinuity within aeromagnetic datasets. Trends are found in the data by identifying regions of textural complexity in the local magnetic response.","platform":"airborne"},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":70,"text":"grab rock sampling from boulders/floats and outcrops, whereas an airborne HELITEM geophysical survey flown over the entire property.","platform":"airborne","year":2025},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":82,"text":"Davidson, S. 1957. Conwest Exploration Company, Airborne Electromagnetic Survey of Trousers Lake Area, Victoria County, New Brunswick. Report 470802; 12 pp. Dimmell, P. M., Hoy, D.","platform":"airborne","year":1957},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":86,"text":", Mapping, Prospecting, Stream Sediment Geochemistry, Soil Geochemistry and Induced Polarization Geophysical Surveys, Claim Nos.","year":1996}],"targets":[{"page":10,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"Overall, 25 conductor axes derived from 234 conductors were identified. These conductive areas are associated with low magnetic signature and elevated radiometric signature, possibly linked to intrusive-related mineralization."},{"page":26,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"Soil anomalies found near zones B and C. An IP survey indicated chargeability anomalies corresponding to zones A and C mineralization. Zone A (Riley Lake showing) contains sphalerite, galena, and chalcopyrite mineralization at the eastern end of Riley Lake."},{"page":30,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"Soil sampling, prospecting. Five areas with IP anomalies coinciding with base metal soil anomalies were identified and tested by diamond drilling. Several DDHs intersected thick silica and sericite alteration zones and disseminated mineralization."},{"page":59,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"The MVI approach directly inverts the magnetic vector rather than the susceptibility, giving a more powerful interpretation that yields the true target location of the magnetic response as compared to conventional inversion methods Furthermore, the local textu"},{"page":77,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"These conductive areas are associated with low magnetic and elevated radiometric signatures, possibly linked to intrusive-related mineralization."}]},"rock":null,"model_params":{"metallurgy":{"routes":[],"traits":["arsenic"],"recoveries":null,"summary":"arsenic-bearing"},"deposit_style":"vein"},"effective_date":"2026-04-06","resource":null,"resource_rows":[],"counts":{"collars":76,"intervals":0,"surveyed_holes":0,"holes_with_intervals":0,"linked":0},"collars":[{"hole":"J023052","e":643057.0,"n":5216810.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":null,"lat":47.089286,"lon":-67.115138},{"hole":"J023058","e":641999.0,"n":5216581.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":null,"lat":47.087455,"lon":-67.129142},{"hole":"J023085","e":647156.0,"n":5223330.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":null,"lat":47.147022,"lon":-67.05903},{"hole":"J023506","e":640391.0,"n":5223281.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":null,"lat":47.148058,"lon":-67.148226},{"hole":"J023502","e":642792.0,"n":5227275.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":null,"lat":47.183463,"lon":-67.115304},{"hole":"J023503","e":642289.0,"n":5226485.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":null,"lat":47.176467,"lon":-67.12219},{"hole":"J023504","e":642245.0,"n":5226457.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":null,"lat":47.176224,"lon":-67.122779},{"hole":"J023060","e":642181.0,"n":5216580.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":null,"lat":47.087407,"lon":-67.126746},{"hole":"J023061","e":642317.0,"n":5216626.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":null,"lat":47.087792,"lon":-67.12494},{"hole":"J023062","e":642153.0,"n":5216755.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":null,"lat":47.088987,"lon":-67.127059},{"hole":"J02